ne.test.mjs`.** It groups the session's work by child session: one box per child (name linking to that child's own page, state, model, an `AICost` cost line, "N of M done") holding the tasks whose folder is the child's or below it, then "This session's own work", sub-grouped by the prompt that asked for it (`SessionOutline.source(session)` is the one place that join lives) with "Other work" for the rest. The children are the union, de-duplicated by session id, of the `sessions` lines of `session.jsonl`, the tree nodes that carry `session`, the day snapshot's `links.children`, and the snapshots whose `parent` is this session's agent; groups are ranked by cost × 0.5^(age days ÷ 2) plus recency, with a "newest first" toggle. A task is one full-width row (open, running, done and dropped icons; the child session's model, cost and state; subtasks folded in), and a done task opens its proof in place. The rows are the Overview's own markup (`SessionOutlineView.item`), not `TaskView`: they carry no start/pause/stop buttons (those live on `TaskView` rows in the Tasks tab), and a folder-only task has no `Task` object for `TaskView` to draw. `SessionTasks` hands it each replay through `on_session`, and the view redraws live. `SessionFeed.js` (+ `SessionFeed.css`, prefix `sfeed-`) is the older flat list and is no longer wired in. `SessionOverview.js` draws the Board tab's four cards side by side (Open, Project, Done, Dropped), with the phone's classes (`MobileRow`, `MobileTaskRow`, `mob-` CSS); `SessionTaskRow.js` is the phone's task row that opens the task's full page and shows its cost. Their styles, and the full-screen mode with two floating buttons (`AISessionDetail.full_screen`, `?full`), are `SessionOverview.css` (prefix `sov-`).
